Notes on the repair: the exact-rate work is retained verbatim (`rdScore`, `lumaCandidateRateQ8`, `preferBPred`, and all existing tests are untouched). The generalized boundary adds one derived quantity — `bPredRDAdvantageMargin(lambda, penalty) = lambda*penalty` — justified by a local invariant: accepting B_PRED rewrites the intra-mode context later macroblocks price against, so only wins strictly exceeding the rate-equivalent of the existing distortion-admission bar (`penalty`, already quantizer-derived and used by `bPredImprovesReconstruction`) are decisive; everything else stays whole-block, preserving exact-tie strictness. The margin is computed in fixed point with checked multiplication that saturates toward rejection, keeps per-macroblock work O(1) and deterministic, changes no public API or Method 0 path, and the new table tests exercise strictly below, exactly at, and strictly above the boundary plus the overflow-safe saturated extreme, without encoding the fixture or the count 51.